{"divisionId":3157,"date":"2024-09-11T00:00:00","number":3,"notes":null,"title":"Social Fund Winter Fuel Payment Regulations 2024","isWhipped":true,"isGovernmentContent":false,"authoritativeContentCount":65,"authoritativeNotContentCount":132,"divisionHadTellers":true,"tellerContentCount":65,"tellerNotContentCount":132,"memberContentCount":63,"memberNotContentCount":130,"sponsoringMemberId":4214,"isHouse":true,"isInquorate":false,"amendmentMotionNotes":"<p>Lord Palmer of Childs Hill moved that this House regrets that the Social Fund Winter Fuel Payment Regulations 2024 (SI 2024/869), laid before the House on 22 August, will remove support from many of the poorest pensioners at the same time as the energy price cap is being lifted; and calls on the Government (1) to take steps to identify those who are eligible for pension credit but do not claim it so that they can receive both benefits; (2) to support vulnerable pensioners this winter; and (3) to take action to end fuel poverty, including with an emergency home insulation programme and a windfall tax on the profits of oil and gas companies. The House divided:</p>","isGovernmentWin":true,"remoteVotingStart":"2024-09-11T19:31:58","remoteVotingEnd":"2024-09-11T19:39:58","divisionWasExclusivelyRemote":false,"contentTellers":[{"memberId":4215,"name":"Lord Stoneham of Droxford","listAs":"Stoneham of Droxford, L.","memberFrom":"Life peer","party":"Liberal Democrat","partyColour":"fc7d0b","partyAbbreviation":"LD","partyIsMainParty":true},{"memberId":2505,"name":"Baroness Harris of Richmond","listAs":"Harris of Richmond, B.","memberFrom":"Life peer","party":"Liberal Democrat","partyColour":"fc7d0b","partyAbbreviation":"LD","partyIsMainParty":true}],"notContentTellers":[{"memberId":4153,"name":"Lord Kennedy of Southwark","listAs":"Kennedy of Southwark, L.","memberFrom":"Life peer","party":"Labour","partyColour":"d50000","partyAbbreviation":"Lab","partyIsMainParty":true},{"memberId":4157,"name":"Baroness Wheeler","listAs":"Whe